  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-12a-2021-p1.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The exponent in the first term is \\(1+2+3 = 6,\\) so the first term is \\(2^6 = 64.\\) The parenthesized sum is \\(2 + 4 + 8 = 14.\\) Therefore the value is \\(64 - 14 = 50.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is B.",
      "hints": [
        "First add the exponents: \\(1+2+3\\)",
        "Evaluate \\(2^6\\) and \\(2^1+2^2+2^3\\) separately, then subtract"
